{
  "_comment": [
    "Condition vocabulary.",
    "",
    "A coin's grade is a Sheldon number, optionally with a plus, and its strike",
    "type says how it was made: PR69+ is strike_type proof with grade 69+, MS65",
    "is business with 65 (docs/specs/item-attributes-design.md). The familiar",
    "MS65 / PR69+ / AU55 is composed for display by app.grades.display and the",
    "database's grade_display().",
    "",
    "`numeric_value` is what makes 'all my 65-and-better Morgans' answerable;",
    "`is_plus` ranks a plus grade half a point above its number. Plus grades",
    "listed here are the points PCGS and NGC give a plus (45-68) and 69+, which",
    "the collection holds; any other is added as `derived` when met.",
    "",
    "Adjectival grades were folded into numbers at the bottom of their standard",
    "range (the owner, 2026-09-16): UNC and BU 60, Choice 63, Gem 65, AU 55, XF",
    "40, VF 20, F 12, VG 8, G 4; the rating as written stays in grade_raw.",
    "Circulated and Ungraded stay unnumbered.",
    "",
    "Note grades keep their own scale and labels (PMG's wording); 3, 2 and 1",
    "are PCGS Banknote's About Good, Fair and Poor.",
    "",
    "Designations follow the services' own terms (item-attributes design,",
    "section 3). NGC's Ultra Cameo is generally synonymous with Deep Cameo and",
    "its DPL equivalent to DMPL, so both are aliases rather than rows; UCAM is",
    "the informal form. FT is NGC's Full Torch (PCGS calls it FB); 5FS and 6FS",
    "are NGC's Jefferson nickel steps, where PCGS's FS means five or more."
  ],
